inely yet (some experimental laundry bags like the “Lunar Outfitters” ones have been tested on station, but not for daily use). The vision is to combine the Tide Infinity detergent with a compact washer-dryer unit for habitats like the Lunar Gateway or a Mars transit vehicle. So you were spot on—the technology is in development, and that often gets reported as “astronauts will wash clothes in space,” but it hasn’t been implemented operationally on the ISS. The current crew still relies on the “wear it until it’s nasty, then throw it into a burning spaceship” method. Thanks for bringing that up; it’s a perfect example of how future-planning news can make it sound like current practice.
